dante 1.4.4 libdsocks: per-thread result buffers for the string helpers

Applies on top of the other dante-*.patch files (lib/tostring.c, lib/util.c
and lib/ipv6.c only).

The address/protocol-to-string helpers (sockaddr2string(), sockshost2string(),
socket2string() and friends) write into a function-static buffer when the
caller passes none, as libdsocks does throughout its logging. Threads of the
program (and sigio(), which runs on any of them) format into the same buffer
at once: garbled log lines, and snprintfn()'s check that its output is
NUL-terminated aborts the program ("an internal error was detected at
../lib/util.c:..., expression \"str[rc] == NUL\""), seen with test/mtstress.c.
The buffers are thread-local now. (A signal handler interrupting the same
helper on the same thread could still clobber it, as before.)

Test: test/mtstress.c (via test/run.sh).

